From: HG680P WiFi Fix – Armbian ARM64 RTL8189FS Driver maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: use the three-argument monitor-channel callback on Linux 6.12

The Linux 6.12 headers used by the tested Armbian 6.12.114-ophub build
declare the cfg80211 set_monitor_channel callback with a net_device
argument and cfg80211_chan_def argument.

The upstream source currently enables that callback signature starting
at Linux 6.13. Lower the version threshold to 6.12 so the driver selects
the matching three-argument callback for the tested 6.12 kernel.

This is a narrow compatibility patch. It does not establish compatibility
with every kernel carrying a 6.12 version number.

Upstream source:
https://github.com/gustiarto/rtl8189fs-armbian

Tested on:
- HG680P (Amlogic S905X)
- Armbian 26.11.0 Ubuntu Noble
- Linux 6.12.114-ophub
- RTL8189FS SDIO 024c:f179

---
diff --git a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
--- a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -6009,4 +6009,4 @@ static int cfg80211_rtw_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy
-#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0))
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0))
 	, struct net_device *dev
 	, struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef
 #elif (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 8, 0))
